@startuml
title ASENT — Integrated Assurance Architecture
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
actor Developer
actor Reviewer
component "Web UI\nReact" as UI
component "API\nFastAPI" as API
component "Run Orchestrator" as ORCH
component "Candidate Context\n& Workspace" as CTX
component "CAVR\nIntegrated dependency analyzer" as CAVR
component "SATRA-RV\nApp and test validator" as SATRA
component "SABLE\nTerraform / IAM analyzer" as SABLE
database "Evidence Store\nSQLite + artifacts" as STORE
component "Evidence Binder\n(snapshot + input hashes)" as BIND
component "Shared Final Gate" as GATE
component "Decision + Findings" as RESULT
Developer --> UI : submit candidate
UI --> API : request assurance
API --> ORCH : create run
ORCH --> CTX : freeze snapshot / resolve inputs
CTX --> ORCH : candidate identity
ORCH --> CAVR : if dependency scope applies
ORCH --> SATRA : if app scope applies
ORCH --> SABLE : if IaC scope applies
CAVR --> STORE : result and evidence
SATRA --> STORE : result and evidence
SABLE --> STORE : result and evidence
STORE --> BIND : select valid evidence
BIND --> GATE : integrity + snapshot/input binding
GATE --> RESULT : ACCEPT / REVIEW / BLOCK
RESULT --> UI : outcome
Reviewer --> UI : inspect evidence
component "Standalone SABLE API / UI" as STAND
STAND --> SABLE : direct module workflow
note bottom of SABLE
Bounded local Terraform/HCL S3 and IAM semantics;
not live AWS validation or universal Terraform support.
end note
note bottom of CAVR
The standalone pip interception API is a separate request path;
it gates requests and does not install or execute package code.
See the dedicated CAVR request sequence.
end note
@enduml
